Forkhammer Lib

This project is a local fork of Warhammer Library by Moo Man.
Upstream: https://github.com/moo-man/WarhammerLibrary-FVTT
Baseline: release 3.5.1, commit 15076301ab1ed4325d237ed0a034d167426c9405.

The upstream Apache License 2.0 is retained verbatim in LICENSE. Original source
attribution comments, including references to adapted D&D5e components, remain
with their respective files.

Fork modifications: distinct Forkhammer package, runtime, settings, asset and
custom-element namespaces; custom-system registration and local builds; Vue
script-editor integration. This fork is independently maintained and is not an
upstream Warhammer Library release. Official Warhammer systems continue to use
Warhammer Library under its original package ID.

Modified source files carry a Forkhammer Lib modification notice. The renamed
entry point and stylesheet derive from src/warhammer-lib.js and
styles/warhammer.scss; static/assets/forkhammer.png is the unmodified upstream
asset under a distinct path. module.json, package.json and package-lock.json were
modified for this fork's identity, local build, registration and Vue dependencies.
static/lang/en.json was modified for fork branding and Vue editor accessibility.
The original README is preserved verbatim in docs/Upstream-Integration.md.
Upstream reporting endpoints and automatic publishing configuration were removed.

The generated runtime also includes Vue runtime packages and Pinia under their
respective MIT licenses. Full dependency copyright and permission notices are
included in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt in each built module. That file is generated
from the packages contributing code to the build, so dependency updates retain
their corresponding notices. These dependencies do not change the upstream
library's Apache-2.0 license.
